  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Thundercat Technology obligated $172M in FY2027 to date. Thundercat Technology received 109 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.6M. Obligations fell 85.3% year over year compared with the prior fiscal period. Historical annual obligations show a peak of $1.2B in FY26 and prior year totals of $916M in FY25, $807M in FY24, $854M in FY23, and $680M in FY22. The Department of Veterans Affairs is the dominant buyer in FY2027 to date with $150M in obligations. Other notable agencies buying from Thundercat Technology in FY2027 to date include the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $8.5M and the Department of Agriculture with $5.6M. The top market by NAICS is Other Computer Related Services with $172M. The company shows concentrated demand this year, with the VA accounting for the vast majority of recorded obligations to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are Thundercat Technology's FY2027 obligations?",
        "body": "Thundercat Technology's obligations are highly concentrated in FY2027 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $150M, which represents most of the $172M total. Other buyers are considerably smaller, with NASA at $8.5M and the Department of Agriculture at $5.6M. The Other Computer Related Services market accounts for $172M of the obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with prior fiscal years?",
        "body": "Thundercat Technology's FY2027 obligations of $172M are down 85.3% year over year. Fiscal year obligations were $1.2B in FY26, $916M in FY25, $807M in FY24, $854M in FY23, and $680M in FY22. The current-year total is partial and reported as fiscal year to date. The change shows a sharp reduction from the prior fiscal year level."
      }
    ]
  },
